## 1. The Big Idea

**Coming off isn't "stopping" — it's a sequenced restart of a system you deliberately switched off, and the single move that ruins it is energizing both stages at once.** The reader should feel, instantly: *there is an order to this, the two tools drive two different parts of the same loop, and the hand-off between them is a hard interlock — not a suggestion.*

The poster makes one abstract idea physical: recovery has **two jobs in a locked order** — **wake the testicles** (gonadotropins, an *external* LH/FSH signal injected at the bottom of the loop) **then restart the brain** (SERMs, which deceive the hypothalamus into driving its *own* signal) — and because the gonadotropins themselves suppress the pituitary, **Stage 1 must power all the way down before Stage 2 powers up.** Run them together and you've floored the accelerator (SERM) and the brake (hCG) at the same time; the brain never gets the "estrogen is low, make your own LH" message. That accelerator/brake interlock is the hero.

## 2. Visual Metaphor or Structure

**A two-stage engine RE-IGNITION SEQUENCER for the HPTA feedback loop.** The body's hormone axis is drawn as a feedback *circuit* — hypothalamus → pituitary → testes (Leydig + Sertoli) — that the cycle has switched **dark**. The instrument re-lights that circuit along a left-to-right restart lane, in a fixed order, gated by a physical interlock that **will not let both stages be energized simultaneously.**

Why this metaphor fits the article's argument better than any alternative:

- The article's spine *is* sequence + interlock. "Wake the testicles first, then restart the brain, and never let the two steps fight each other" is literally a startup procedure with a safety interlock.
- The two tools act on **two different nodes of the same loop** — gonadotropins inject an external signal at the *testes* (bottom); SERMs act at the *brain* (top). A circuit you re-light from the bottom up makes that spatial split obvious.
- The load-bearing rule ("stop hCG/hMG before the SERM phase") is the article's own accelerator-vs-brake image. A **mutual-exclusion interlock** — a single drive bus that physically rejects both inputs at once — turns that sentence into geometry.
- "Clearance sets the clock" becomes the **runway** the sequence cannot start its brain-phase on until it's clear.

This is deliberately distinct from **3.2's Gantt** (a forward *calendar* of a whole year): here the device is the **hand-off gate between two interlocked stages**, not the timeline. The phases have honest durations, but the poster's gravity is the interlock, not the schedule.

## 3. Layout Description

**Orientation: landscape.** The restart reads left→right as the dominant axis (clearance → Stage 1 → interlock → Stage 2 → verify), which matches both the *time* of recovery and the *bottom-up then top-down* relighting of the loop. (Flips compositionally from 4.4's landscape *hydraulic bench* by being an all-electrical wiring/ignition schematic — no fluid, no vessels.)

**Left edge — THE DORMANT LOOP (the "before" state, ~18% width).** A tall vertical feedback column, drawn **dark/greyed-out**: HYPOTHALAMUS (top) → PITUITARY → TESTES (bottom, with a small "shrunk / quiet" tell — reduced volume glyph, *not* a cartoon). A faint inbound arrow labelled `exogenous androgen → brain sees plenty → GnRH off` shows *why* it's dark. A small upstream **pilot-light** chip sits beside it: **INTRA-CYCLE MAINTENANCE — the easy path** (`low-dose hCG kept on *during* the cycle → testicles never go fully dormant; far easier to maintain sensitivity than to resurrect it`). The pilot light is the only thing lit in this otherwise-dark column = the article's "smart default."

**The restart lane (the main body, read left→right):**

1. **CLEARANCE RUNWAY (the clock).** A horizontal bar at the lane's start = the wait for the gear to leave the system. A small **ester-length dial** (`short ester / oral = days · enanthate-cypionate = ~2 wks · undecanoate-deca = longer`) sets the runway length. Caption: `the longer the ester, the longer you wait` and `last dose + clearance = SERM start date`. A dashed note: *Stage-1 wake-up may overlap the tail of clearance; the SERM phase waits for a clean runway.*

2. **STAGE 1 — WAKE THE TESTICLES (~2–3 wks).** Lights the **bottom** of the loop from an **EXTERNAL injected signal**. Two feed-lines drop in at the testes node:
   - `hCG → mimics LH → Leydig cells → testosterone + testicular volume` (`~500–1,000 IU EOD` wake dose, vs the lighter `~250–500 IU 2–3×/wk` maintenance — doses as small annotations only).
   - `hMG → mimics FSH → Sertoli cells → sperm` (contains real FSH → expensive → reserved for fertility; `~75 IU 2–3×/wk`).
   - **Critical label on this stage: the BRAIN STAYS DARK.** A status flag reads `external signal — pituitary still quiet`. The lit colour here is the instrument's **"borrowed / external" accent**, visibly *not* the self-driven success colour (see §5) — this is the conceptual heart: the loop is being driven *from outside*.
   - An amber caution badge: `DON'T MEGA-DOSE — one big 5,000 IU hit spikes aromatase, drives estrogen, desensitizes the Leydig cells you're trying to wake. Frequent small doses win.`

3. **THE INTERLOCK GATE (the hero object, dead-centre).** A single **drive bus / hand-off coupling** between Stage 1 and Stage 2 that is physically keyed to accept **only one input at a time.** Drawn as a two-position selector or a keyed coupling: when the Stage-1 (gonadotropin) line is engaged, the Stage-2 (SERM) port is mechanically blocked, and vice-versa. The instruction stamped across it: `STOP hCG / hMG → THEN START SERMs`. Beneath it, a compact **ghosted FAULT inset** = the single red object (see §5): both lines energized at once, rendered as an **accelerator + brake pressed together**, with the loop staying dark and the caption `gonadotropins suppress the pituitary → run them into the SERM window and the brain never gets its "make your own LH" cue → months suppressed while believing you're recovering.`

4. **STAGE 2 — RESTART THE BRAIN (~4 wks, tapering).** Now the **top** of the loop re-lights, driven by the brain itself. A feed-line acts at the **hypothalamus**:
   - `SERMs → block estrogen feedback → brain reads "estrogen low" → ramps its OWN GnRH → LH/FSH`.
   - `Enclomiphene` flagged as preferred (`~12.5–25 → taper 6.25–12.5 mg/day`) with a micro-note: *trans-isomer only — drops the zuclomiphene mood/visual sides of Clomid* (a Part 4.2 within-family-selection callback).
   - `Tamoxifen ~20 → 10 mg/day` — used where gyno is a concern (blocks estrogen at breast tissue).
   - A small side chip: `Triptorelin — single-shot GnRH agonist, one big pituitary release; potent, timing-unforgiving — know it exists.`
   - Amber grace-note: `keep SOME estrogen — it's part of the feedback signal (libido, joints, bone). Manage the rebound; don't crush it with an AI or you blunt the recovery.`
   - As this stage lights, the loop's drive colour switches from the **external accent** to the **self-driven** treatment — the visual payoff of "the brain is doing it now."

5. **PHASE 3 — HOLD & VERIFY (the gate that earns the green).** A bloodwork verdict meter, not a feelings check. Two reads compared: **baseline** (Test, LH, FSH, SHBG — "know your hole") vs **~4–6 wks post-final-SERM**. Three lamp states:
   - **RECOVERED (green — the ONLY green on the poster):** `LH & FSH climbed · Test healthy WITHOUT exogenous help → the loop holds on its own.`
   - **PARTIAL (amber):** `LH up but Test lagging → testes need more time / a short gonadotropin nudge.`
   - **NOT RECOVERED (amber-into-grey):** `LH still flat → the brain hasn't restarted → don't "wait and hope," reassess with a physician.`
   - Stamp: `the-number-is-the-boss` (Part 4.1 callback).

**Foundation rail (a thin substrate under the entire lane).** **THE SUPPORT LAYER — the floor, not the engine.** D3 + zinc (synthesis base) · boron (↓SHBG → more free T) · Tongkat Ali + KSM-66 ashwagandha (LH signalling, cortisol) · nutrition (hold maintenance/slight deficit — the SERM appetite surge is how people go soft; *80% retention* expectation) · training (hold the stimulus, drop the volume to match low-androgen recovery). Drawn explicitly *beneath* the drive path, wired to nothing on the loop = "makes the crash manageable, restarts nothing."

**FERTILITY BRANCH (a fork off Stage 1).** A labelled spur: `GOAL = A CHILD → the one case the two gonadotropins run TOGETHER.` hCG (`~500–1,000 IU EOD`) **+** hMG (`~75–150 IU EOD`, pushed harder/longer), scorecard = **semen analysis**, not testosterone. Note: *can layer onto a TRT base, but fully hopping off gives the best odds* — and `"do you want kids, and when" is a PRE-cycle decision (Part 1)`, not a someday-problem.

**Bottom-right caveat plate (quiet, amber).** `Recovery is not guaranteed and not symmetric — longer suppressed · older · more aggressive compounds = less complete, slower bounce-back. Some land lower than they started; a few stay on lifelong TRT, which should be a chosen destination, not an accident. The surest protection is the restraint that came before PCT.`

**Eye path:** dark dormant loop (left, "this is off") → runway clock → Stage 1 lights the bottom from outside → the **interlock gate snaps the eye to centre** (the rule + the red fault) → Stage 2 lights the top and the colour flips to self-driven → the verify gate is the only green = the destination. The support rail and fertility fork read as second-pass detail.

